  {
    "id": "521f171853bc3d4cc2014bd8",
    "path": "datafusion_sql::unparser::Unparser::with_extension_unparsers",
    "name": "with_extension_unparsers",
    "owner": "datafusion_sql::unparser::Unparser",
    "crate": "datafusion-sql",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn with_extension_unparsers(self, extension_unparsers: Vec<Arc<dyn UserDefinedLogicalNodeUnparser>>) -> Self",
    "docs": "Add a custom unparser for user defined logical nodes\n\nDataFusion allows user to define custom logical nodes. This method allows to add custom child unparsers for these nodes.\nImplementation of [`UserDefinedLogicalNodeUnparser`] can be added to the root unparser to handle custom logical nodes.\n\nThe child unparsers are called iteratively.\nThere are two methods in [`Unparser`] will be called:\n- `extension_to_statement`: This method is called when the custom logical node is a custom statement.\n  If multiple child unparsers return a non-None value, the last unparsing result will be returned.\n- `extension_to_sql`: This method is called when the custom logical node is part of a statement.\n  If multiple child unparsers are registered for the same custom logical node, all of them will be called in order.",
